  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Add the native C frame executor and a Rust Metal CLI for trusted exported capacity ladders.",
  "regressions": [
    "Native C tests compile actual kernels and cover growth after an existing frame, skipped undersized variants, relocated persistent regions, step limits, exhausted capacity, failed growth compilation, invalid variant meanings and poisoned partial commits.",
    "CLI validates manifests before resolving kernel/storage paths and rejects invalid variant directories.",
    "The delayed-growth diagnostic runs 120 frames on C and Metal, grows on frame 48 and matches the fresh Rust trajectory exactly across all frames. This diagnostic does not replace registered current-source runtime evidence."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Both executors interpret small control counters on the host while generated kernels perform all physics. C uses native host storage; Metal migrates persistent regions with device blits.",
    "Public arbitrary scene upload and backend selection, registered runtime scenes, complete handoff validation and Ascend execution integration remain outstanding."
  ]
}
